        "final_text": "**Investigation Summary**\n\nThe only quantitative evidence available is the per\u2011fold AUCs from the out\u2011of\u2011fold (OOF) predictions:\n\n| Fold | AUC   |\n|------|-------|\n| 2023 | 0.690708 |\n| 2024 | 0.680062 |\n| 2025 | 0.689827 |\n\nThe spread between the lowest and highest fold is only ~0.01, which is negligible relative to the overall AUC (~0.683).  \nThis observation directly contradicts **Hypothesis\u202f1** (distribution shift between folds), which predicts significant variation in fold\u2011wise performance.  \n**Hypothesis\u202f2** (data leakage inflating training metrics) cannot be confirmed or refuted because we lack training\u2011set performance data. The OOF metrics alone do not reveal leakage.\n\n**Conclusion**  \nThe model\u2019s underperformance on OOF data is not due to a large distribution shift across folds. The cause remains uncertain; further diagnostics are required, particularly comparing training vs. OOF metrics and inspecting potential leakage sources.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"conclusion\": \"No evidence of significant distribution shift across folds; data leakage remains untested.\",\n  \"status_recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"hypothesis_id\": \"147726b7c78444669751d39f7c045be5\",\n      \"status\": \"rejected\",\n      \"basis\": \"per_split_auc variation < 0.01\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hypothesis_id\": \"b9b8a73dc82c41238f65114f9e251958\",\n      \"status\": \"inconclusive\",\n      \"basis\": \"training metrics not available\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"Lack of training\u2011set performance data prevents assessment of leakage.\",\n    \"Small fold\u2011wise variation may still mask subtle distribution differences.\",\n    \"Other factors (e.g., model capacity, feature quality) not evaluated.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommended_next\": \"Compute training AUCs, compare to OOF AUCs; perform feature\u2011target correlation analysis to detect leakage; evaluate calibration across folds.\"\n}\n```",
